        "description": "Behavioral requirements for nodes participating in the DAS custody protocol, including custody obligations, sampling behavior, reconstruction, and cross-seeding.",
        "invariants": [
          {"id": "INV-DAS-CP-001", "text": "Nodes custodying a custody group MUST custody all columns in that group."},
          {"id": "INV-DAS-CP-002", "text": "When syncing, a node MUST backfill columns from all of its custody groups."},
          {"id": "INV-DAS-CP-003", "text": "Custody selection is public and deterministic via get_custody_groups."},
          {"id": "INV-DAS-CP-004", "text": "A node stores custodied columns for the duration of the pruning period."},
          {"id": "INV-DAS-CP-005", "text": "Sampling is successful if the node retrieves all selected columns."},
          {"id": "INV-DAS-CP-006", "text": "sampling_size = max(SAMPLES_PER_SLOT, custody_group_count) for each slot."},
          {"id": "INV-DAS-CP-007", "text": "If a node obtains 50%+ of all columns, it SHOULD reconstruct the full matrix via recover_matrix."},
          {"id": "INV-DAS-CP-008", "text": "After reconstruction, nodes MUST expose new columns as if received over the network."},
          {"id": "INV-DAS-CP-009", "text": "If subscribed to the subnet of a reconstructed column, the node MUST send the DataColumnSidecar to mesh neighbors."}
